    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1052">

                <pb facs="0972" n="658" xml:id="pg658"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/8014</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Spring Rice</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Counselor for the Department
                            of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-07">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">October 7, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Lansing</hi>: I did not fail to inform Sir E. Grey of the contents of your personal
                    and confidential note of the 5th instant, calling attention to the presence of
                    the British cruisers Lancaster and <hi rendition="#italic">Suffolk</hi> in close
                    proximity to the harbour of New York. I now beg to inform you that I have
                    received a telegram from Sir E. Grey in
                    reply, stating that instructions have been issued to the British Admiral to take
                    the necessary steps to prevent a repetition of these incidents.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cecil Spring Rice</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
